<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Louis the Younger</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">835–882</span> · <a href="/centuries/9th-century">9th century</a> · Also known as Louis III the Younger</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Louis the Younger was king of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/east-francia">East Francia</a> from 876 to 882, a son of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/louis-the-german">Louis the German</a>. He ruled <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/saxony">Saxony</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/franconia">Franconia</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/thuringia">Thuringia</a> and later <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bavaria">Bavaria</a>, and in 876 defeated his uncle <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/charles-the-bald">Charles the Bald</a> at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/andernach">Andernach</a> when Charles tried to seize the western lands of his inheritance. He married Liutgard, daughter of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/saxons">Saxon</a> count Liudolf, and was buried, like his father, at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/lorsch">Lorsch</a> Abbey.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/louis-the-younger.jpg" alt="Louis the Younger" width="194" height="248" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Ekkehard von Aura · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Louis_the_Younger_of_Saxony.PNG" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
